==============================================================================
C3  conditional growth of the least cycle length with the verification bound N
==============================================================================
  If |log_2 3 - p/q| >= c q^(-mu) for all q, then a cycle with all elements >= N has 0 < K/L - alpha <
  delta_N ~ 1/(3N ln 2), hence L > (3 c N ln 2)^(1/mu).  Lang-Waldschmidt (two logarithms, fixed
  algebraic 2 and 3) gives mu = 2 + eps; the computed least L tracks sqrt(N):
    N = 2^ 40: L_min =             10781274   L_min/sqrt(N) =    10.2818   log L_min / log N = 0.5841
    N = 2^ 50: L_min =             64497107   L_min/sqrt(N) =     1.9222   log L_min / log N = 0.5189
    N = 2^ 60: L_min =            397573379   L_min/sqrt(N) =     0.3703   log L_min / log N = 0.4761
    N = 2^ 68: L_min =          72057431991   L_min/sqrt(N) =     4.1943   log L_min / log N = 0.5304
    N = 2^ 71: L_min =          72057431991   L_min/sqrt(N) =     1.4829   log L_min / log N = 0.5080
    N = 2^ 75: L_min =         137528045312   L_min/sqrt(N) =     0.7076   log L_min / log N = 0.4933
    N = 2^ 80: L_min =        2396860564955   L_min/sqrt(N) =     2.1799   log L_min / log N = 0.5141
    N = 2^ 90: L_min =       64021008208555   L_min/sqrt(N) =     1.8196   log L_min / log N = 0.5096
    N = 2^100: L_min =     3332857981044265   L_min/sqrt(N) =     2.9602   log L_min / log N = 0.5157
  Unconditionally: Lagarias 2009 Lemma 2.2 (from Rhin 1987): |log_3 2 - p/q| >= q^(-14.3)/1200 for all q >= 1.
  With |log_3 2 - L/K| < (L/K) delta_N / alpha this gives the fully explicit, unconditional bound
    N = 2^71: K > 21.3553  (versus the continued-fraction truth above)
    N = 2^100: K > 87.0936  (versus the continued-fraction truth above)
    N = 2^200: K > 11094.1  (versus the continued-fraction truth above)
  so proved irrationality measures are useless at the present N; asymptotically they give L >> N^(1/14.3)
  (explicit) or N^(1/8.616) (Rhin, asymptotic [R]), against the LW prediction N^(1/2) that the record tracks.

==============================================================================
C4  the gate barrier: lower bounds for D = |2^K - 3^L| (log_2 D - K shown)
==============================================================================
  abc on 3^L + D = 2^K (coprime, rad(2^K 3^L D) <= 6 rad(D) <= 6D):  2^K <= K_eps (6D)^(1+eps),
     so log2 D >= K/(1+eps) - log2 6 - log2(K_eps)/(1+eps)   [shown with the optimistic K_eps = 1].
  Baker's explicit abc (c < (6/5) N (log N)^w / w!, N = rad, w = #primes):  D >= (5/36) 2^K w!/(K ln2 + ln6)^w
     with w = omega(D) + 2 (shown for w = 3 and for the worst admissible w ~ K ln2/ln K).
  Ellison 1971 Thm 3: D > 2^K e^(-K/10) for K not in {1..11,13,14,16,19,27} [P].
  Rhin 1987 (via Simons-de Weger Lemma 12 [R]): |u0 + u1 log2 + u2 log3| >= H^(-13.3), so D >= c 2^K K^(-13.3).
  truth at the record clocks K = p_n: log2 D = K + log2|1 - 2^(-(K - L alpha))|, from the continued fraction.

   K            abc eps=.1   abc eps=.01   expl.abc w=3   expl.abc worst   Ellison     C=13.3      truth(record clock)
              65        -8.494        -3.229        -16.91          -36.56      -9.378       -80.1      -6.4551
           24727         -2250        -247.4        -42.46           -8096       -3567      -194.1     -15.7461
          301994    -2.746e+04         -2993        -53.29       -8.46e+04  -4.357e+04      -242.1     -23.8860
       272500658    -2.477e+07    -2.698e+06        -82.74      -5.565e+07  -3.931e+07      -372.7     -29.0580
     10439860591    -9.491e+08    -1.034e+08        -98.52      -1.873e+09  -1.506e+09      -442.6     -36.5236
   8573543875303    -7.794e+11    -8.489e+10        -127.6      -1.265e+12  -1.237e+12      -571.4     -43.7861
  683381996816440    -6.213e+13    -6.766e+12        -146.5      -9.065e+13  -9.859e+13      -655.4     -49.4134
  Reading: plain abc loses a factor 2^(eps K/(1+eps)) -- exponentially worse than the proved Baker-type
  bounds (polynomial or quasi-polynomial loss) and than the truth (~ K^-1); it beats only Ellison's
  exponential-loss bound for eps < 0.168.  Explicit abc is polynomial only when omega(D) is small.
  PROVED (comparison): every cycle-length or cycle-element bound obtained from 'gate lower bound +
  product identity + verification' is monotone in the gate bound, so abc adds nothing to Baker there.

==============================================================================
C5  abc and the two-block parity prefix 1^k 0^l
==============================================================================
  n has T-parity prefix 1^k 0^l  <=>  n = 2^k A - 1 with 3^k A = 1 + 2^l B (A odd).  abc on (1, 2^l B, 3^k A):
  3^k A <= K_eps (6AB)^(1+eps) and B < 3^k A/2^l give log2 A >= l(1+eps)/(1+2eps) - eps k log2(3)/(1+2eps) - O_eps(1),
  i.e. n >= c_eps 2^(k + (1-eps) l - 1.59 eps k)  (Proposition R2 of the note; Rozier's Thm 2.1 is the prefix 1^k 0 1^(j-k-1)).
  Unconditionally A_min(k,l) = (3^(-k) mod 2^l) can be tiny only when k is huge: A = 1 needs 2^(l-2) | k.

  worst cases of log2(A_min)/l over 1 <= k <= 2l, for l = 8..48 (exact):
