==============================================================================
C6  Catalan and Pillai for the bases 2 and 3 (finite checks)
==============================================================================
  |2^K - 3^L| = 1 with K, L >= 1, K <= 400: [(1, 1), (2, 1), (3, 2)]  (Gersonides/Levi ben Gershon; Mihailescu in general)
  values c = 3^L - 2^K with 0 < |c| <= 10^4 in the box K <= 400, L < 260: 124 values;
  values attained twice or more: {-13: [(4, 1), (8, 5)], -7: [(3, 0), (4, 2)], -5: [(3, 1), (5, 3)], -1: [(1, 0), (2, 1)], 1: [(1, 1), (3, 2)]}
  (consistent with the cited Pillai-type theorems for 3^x - 2^y = c; the note gives the exact statements.)
  Collatz relevance: a gate value D = 2^K - 3^L determines its clock for |D| > 13 in this box; the carry
  condition D | B(w) is untouched by any fixed-c Pillai statement.

==============================================================================
C7  Terras's coefficient stopping time: sigma(n) = tau(n) for 2 <= n <= 2000000
==============================================================================
  mismatches: 0; max tau = 224
  Implications (PROVED in the note, elementary):
   (i)  CST => no nontrivial positive cycle: the minimum m of such a cycle has tau(m) <= K < sigma(m) = infinity.
   (ii) T1 => tau(n) < infinity for all n >= 1: if tau(n) = infinity, T^j(n) >= n for all j and the orbit
        is not eventually periodic (a positive cycle forces 3^a_j/2^j -> 0), so it diverges.
   (iii) CST & (tau finite) => Collatz (sigma(n) = tau(n) < infinity for every n >= 2, then induction);
        hence CST & T1 => Collatz, and Collatz <=> NC & T1.

DONE cycles

