==============================================================================
B5  swap principle SP(rho): Theta_S(rho) = sum_{s in S} rho^s in Q_2 is irrational for every
==============================================================================
      non-eventually-periodic S.  rho = 2^L/3^a: PROVED for 3^a < 2^L (Lemma L); implied by PC
      for 2^L < 3^a, a < L (open, HARD); FALSE at a = L (rho = 2/3) by Mahler's map:
  D = odd positions of the M-orbit of 1 (first 20: [0, 2, 3, 7, 8, 10, 13, 14, 16, 18, 21, 22, 24, 27, 29, 35, 36, 38, 46, 48]), non-periodic (the orbit is increasing).
  Theta_D(2/3) = sum_(d in D) (2/3)^d == -3 (mod 2^4000): True
  So SP(2/3) is FALSE: a non-periodic 0/1 series in base 2/3 has the rational 2-adic value -3.
  (Every positive integer g gives such a witness: Theta_{D_g}(2/3) = -3g, THM-2228's carry identity.)

